diff --git a/CHANGELOG.md b/CHANGELOG.md
index 56f1479..e4cd128 100644
--- a/CHANGELOG.md
+++ b/CHANGELOG.md
@@ -25,13 +25,17 @@
 - Standalone-режим: репозиторий собирается и запускается без соседнего `services-base` (убраны extra `cli-platform`, uv source, Docker additional_context и CI checkout). Token-режим CLI без `sdlc-cli-core` выдаёт понятную ошибку; запуск без `AUTH_ISSUER` работает без авторизации.
 
 ### Fixed
+- Agent create/update keeps drafts frozen after lost responses, 5xx and malformed
+  or mismatched ACKs. Explicit no-cache catalogue readback reconciles the result
+  without replay; confirmed 401/403/404 disables CRUD and retains the values.
+  Validation/conflict errors remain editable. No API or runtime changes.
 - Docker frontend stage includes the pinned `.base-revision` before recording
   product fingerprints; container metadata now attests the same runtime inputs
   as the clean checkout. Jinja/React routes and the active skills catalog are unchanged.
 - Agent editors use Base SSR controls and draft protection for navigation and
   disclosure/cancel. Pending create/update locks fields and actions and rejects
   direct duplicate handlers; rejected HTTP responses cannot announce success.
-  Unknown create/update outcome reconciliation remains a separate follow-up.
+  Unknown create/update outcome reconciliation is covered by the subsequent fix above.
 - Jinja deletion confirmations use the shared Base SSR native dialog instead
   of a local modal shell. Pending callbacks keep the dialog locked until API
   acknowledgement; uncertain deletes block repeat writes across cancel/reopen
diff --git a/docs/UI_UX_MAP.md b/docs/UI_UX_MAP.md
index 7d02a12..db26692 100644
--- a/docs/UI_UX_MAP.md
+++ b/docs/UI_UX_MAP.md
@@ -99,3 +99,21 @@ SSR assets сохраняют собственную byte-for-byte drift про
 Это узкий кандидат, не закрытие полного agent/workflow lifecycle. Unknown outcome,
 read-only reconcile, authoritative ACK payload и terminal 401/403/404 create/update
 ещё OPEN. Release/images/SSO и полный quality gate фиксируются отдельным evidence.
+
+## Agent Write Lifecycle Candidate 2026-10-06
+
+Последующий source-кандидат закрывает create/update unknown lifecycle редакторов
+агентов: поля и CRUD остаются заблокированными после потерянного ответа, 5xx,
+неполного ACK или несовпадения id/значений. Отдельное действие сверяет существующий
+GET `/api/agents` без cache и никогда не повторяет запись. Отрицательная сверка и
+ошибка каталога сохраняют черновик и блокировку. Create не подтверждается старым
+id из исходного списка; ACK проверяет совпадение `agent_id` и возвращённого объекта.
+401/403/404 показываются отдельными Base states без CRUD/retry записи; 409/422
+сохраняют редактируемый черновик. Доступная проверка получает фокус после unknown,
+после подтверждённого update фокус возвращается summary редактора.
+
+Используются существующие Base SSR controls/states/draft guard; доменная сверка
+остаётся в продукте. Публичные API, схема БД, SSO и runtime pins не меняются.
+Это source/fixture acceptance, не приёмка фактических images или SSO. Lifecycle
+редактора workflows и общая image/route/theme/README matrix остаются отдельными
+незавершёнными пунктами программы.
diff --git a/docs/plans/2026-10-06-agent-write-lifecycle.md b/docs/plans/2026-10-06-agent-write-lifecycle.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..1716915
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/plans/2026-10-06-agent-write-lifecycle.md
@@ -0,0 +1,39 @@
+# Agent Write Lifecycle Source Candidate
+
+## Scope
+
+Use Base SSR states, controls and draft guard for the existing agent editor.
+Keep domain reconciliation in Workflow; do not change API, database or auth.
+This follows the previous agent draft candidate and does not imply runtime release.
+
+## Acceptance
+
+- Pending locks fields/actions and rejects duplicate direct handlers.
+- Transport failures, 408/5xx, invalid JSON and incomplete/mismatched successful
+  responses freeze the draft. Cancel/reopen cannot unlock or replay the write.
+- An explicit GET catalogue check uses no-store; only matching authoritative
+  fields and a valid id acknowledge persistence. Create excludes original ids.
+- Negative/failed readback retains the draft; no automatic write retry.
+- Confirmed 401/403/404 disables CRUD; validation/conflict rejection keeps edits.
+- Whitespace-only names show a persistent localized validation error; invalid
+  launch keys cannot submit through either the form or direct handlers. HTML
+  patterns compile with the native `v` flag; escaping changes no API value set.
+- Acknowledged update sets field defaults from the server and returns focus.
+  Acknowledged create keeps the existing navigation guard for other dirty forms.
+- Browser tests cover desktop/mobile, three themes, actual disposable POST with
+  a lost/malformed response, direct duplicate calls, stale and failed GET readback.
+- Run the full Python/PostgreSQL/coverage/Ruff/mypy/resource-warning gate,
+  frontend checks, SSR drift and complete isolated browser suite before commit.
+- Localization checks parse Jinja/HTML page labels (including macro arguments),
+  excluding script/style identifiers. Existing API DTO names are not UI labels;
+  regression cases preserve the prohibition on executor-specific visible names.
+  Rendered HTML is not reinterpreted as Jinja; literal template syntax stays
+  visible. Known errors use one persistent inline state, not a duplicate toast.
+
+## Remaining Release Work
+
+Workflow editor lifecycle remains separate. Actual immutable runtime images,
+SSO/roles, all route/theme/width checks, README capture provenance and mirror
+refresh require fresh evidence; fixture screenshots are not README release images.
+
+Pattern syntax follows the [HTML Standard](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/input.html#the-pattern-attribute).
